From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kurt Fuchs <contact@fuchskurt.eu>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:37:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] coreboot: drop dead TPM-only code and unused build
 dependencies

The locked build leaves out the `tpm` feature, so the TCPA event-log
helpers in acpi.rs were compiled but never called, and the TpmLogInfo
address/size fields were never read. Gate the helpers on `tpm` (their only
caller already is) and allow the unread fields when TPM is off; the CBMEM
table parser keeps recording the log in every build.

crabefi-coreboot's build.rs does not use its `cc` dependency; remove it
and its now-unused lockfile entries.
---
 Cargo.lock                     | 23 -----------------------
 crabefi-coreboot/Cargo.toml    |  1 -
 crabefi-coreboot/src/acpi.rs   |  4 ++--
 crabefi-coreboot/src/tables.rs |  3 +++
 4 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Cargo.lock b/Cargo.lock
index 907f968..35a3baf 100644
--- a/Cargo.lock
+++ b/Cargo.lock
@@ -69,16 +69,6 @@ version = "1.5.0"
 source = "registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"
 checksum = "1fd0f2584146f6f2ef48085050886acf353beff7305ebd1ae69500e27c67f64b"
 
-[[package]]
-name = "cc"
-version = "1.9.0"
-source = "registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"
-checksum = "877bf67ac8e52449eb2f9e98a344ea163beb70dd1f9eebe3cc5357dcfeaee4df"
-dependencies = [
- "find-msvc-tools",
- "shlex",
-]
